# Dev-run artifacts, not part of the plugin's own content — see PLUGIN_BUILD_CONTEXT.md's
# "Stray dev artifacts" note. logs/ gets written to by whichever MCP server process happens to be
# launched with this directory as its working directory (e.g. the Authoring Plugin's jar), not by
# Companion itself.
logs/

# Local Claude Code session/permission overrides — machine-specific, not meant to ship with the
# plugin (per-team-member .claude/settings.local.json already documents its own contents).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Live OAuth session for the Pega Infinity Authoring Plugin's MCP server — contains a real access
# token and refresh token for a client's Pega instance. This directory is written by that plugin's
# own MCP server (not Companion) whenever it happens to run with this folder as its working
# directory, same as logs/ above. NEVER commit this — it is a live credential, not plugin content.
.infinity-rules-mcp/

# Standalone-jar / bytecode-extraction scratch work from reverse-engineering the Authoring Plugin
# during analysis sessions — Pegasystems' own compiled classes, not Companion's content, and not
# meant to ever be tracked even if it reappears locally.
jx/
